    "notes": "Source file: Ecosystem-Statistics-UPI-Top-50-member-performance-2026-Jul-Remitter.xlsx, sheet Sheet20. Remitter (payer-side) table, which is the correct side for issuer-decline modelling.\nAll 48 issuing banks retained - no volume cutoff applied, so there is no threshold to justify. Volume-weighted aggregates are stable across cutoffs (TD 0.374%-0.402% from top-15 through full table), so the choice does not drive downstream results.\nTwo non-bank entities excluded: Tri O Tech Solutions Private Limited and One Mobikwik Systems Limited. Both report 100.00% approved with zero BD and zero TD, which is characteristic of a technology provider rather than an issuing bank. Together they are 231.70 Mn of 25,897.80 Mn (0.89%). Including them would grant a non-issuer a volume share and a perfect approval rate, biasing the world's aggregates upward.\nPercentages in the source are stored as text (\"90.29%\") and were divided by 100 to rates. Every row satisfies approved + BD + TD = 1.0 within NPCI's two-decimal rounding.\nAEPS BD/TD file deliberately not used: Aadhaar-enabled banking-correspondent transactions are a different rail with materially different decline behaviour.\n"
